// A coral grew beside a rock post; the post cast a shadow through the growth, and the shadow points away from the stone.
name Shadow
rule B1/S12345678
steps 5
hint Here nothing dies, and a cell is born only beside exactly one neighbour, so growth is thin and easily blocked. A rock post stands in this coral. Growth is light: the post cast a shadow, and the shadow falls away from the stone.
tip Cells that could not be born because the post stood between them and the stone are missing on the post's far side. The stone is on the near side, on the floor, two from the post.
intro Everything ever born here is still here, thin as coral. And a post of rock stood in the middle of it while it grew.
outro The coral remembers the post as a shadow. So does the ground remember you.
say wake|The blocks up this shaft do not like being stood on. Keep moving.
say plant|Beside the post, on its lit side. If you are wrong the shadow will fall the wrong way.
say grow|Five generations. Watch how it goes around the post.
say found|The shadow fell where it should. Up the coral, then.
say die|Everything that grew here died once too.
